```javascript
function toTitleCase(str) {
  const result = [];
  for (let word of str.split(' ')) {
    result.push(word.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + word.slice(1).toLowerCase());
  }
  return result.join(' ');
}
```

* **Using regular expressions with lookbehind:**
```javascript
function toTitleCase(str) {
  return str.replace(/(?<!\b)\w/g, (txt) => txt.toUpperCase());
}
```

These variations achieve the same result as the original function, but they use different approaches.

